        "net9.0": { "description": ".NET 9" }
      }
    },
    "enableLogging": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "datatype": "bool",
      "defaultValue": "yes"
    },
    "maxRetries": {
      "type": "parameter",
      "datatype": "int",
      "defaultValue": "abc"
    },
    "computed1": {
      "type": "computed"
    },
    "generated1": {
      "type": "generated"
    }
  },
  "postActions": [
    {
      "description": "Restore packages"
    }
  ]
}
```

I'm noticing some issues here—the maxRetries parameter has an integer datatype but its default value is "abc", which isn't a valid integer. I'm also seeing that `maxRetries` has an invalid default value, `computed1` is missing its value expression, `generated1` lacks a generator field, and the post-action is missing an actionId. Beyond the errors, there are several warnings about missing metadata like `sourceName` and parameter descriptions, plus suggestions to add a template description, default name, tags, and manual instructions on the post-action.
